      "type": "explain",
      "title": "F and G",
      "body": "The letters carry on to the right. **F** is the white key just to the left of each group of three black keys, and **G** is the next white key after it.\n\n**Why it matters:** with F and G, you can find five of the seven letters. Lots of songs start on G.",
